Subject: [EXPERIMENT] ASoC: x1e80100: keep the reference PA range on the protected route

The machine driver caps the two Denali PA volume controls at 6 ("until
active speaker protection is in place"). The reference-render fixture is
the protected route and validates PA Volume 24 (+27 dB) on both amplifiers
with VI/CPS live; keep the upstream damage cap only when that route is
not explicitly selected. The RX digital -3 dB ceiling stays unchanged.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
@@ -44,5 +44,13 @@ static int x1e80100_snd_init(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd)
 		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "WSA2 WSA_RX0 Digital Volume", 81);
 		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "WSA2 WSA_RX1 Digital Volume", 81);
-		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "SpkrLeft PA Volume", 6);
-		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "SpkrRight PA Volume", 6);
+		/* The protected reference route validates PA Volume 24 on both
+		 * amps with live VI/CPS. Keep the upstream damage cap when that
+		 * route is not explicitly selected.
+		 */
+		if (!of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,denali") ||
+		    !of_property_read_bool(card->dev->of_node,
+					  "microsoft,denali-fullio-reference-render")) {
+			snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "SpkrLeft PA Volume", 6);
+			snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "SpkrRight PA Volume", 6);
+		}
 		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "WooferLeft PA Volume", 6);
